# ShengRi Frontend Design Rules

## Tech Stack

- React 18 + TypeScript
- react-admin 5 (admin panel framework)
- MUI 5 (Material UI) — `@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material`
- Emotion (`@emotion/react`, `@emotion/styled`) for CSS-in-JS
- Vite for build tooling
- react-router-dom 6.28.1

## Design System

### Brand Colors

Primary palette derived from traditional Chinese aesthetics (cinnabar/vermillion tones):

```
primary.main:   #c44520  (朱砂红 — cinnabar red)
primary.light:  #d86a4a
primary.dark:   #8a3016
secondary.main: #dca310  (金色 — gold)
secondary.light: #e6b840
secondary.dark: #9a720b
background.default: #fdf8f4 (warm off-white)
background.paper:   #ffffff
text.primary:   #2d2d2d
text.secondary: #666666
```

### Typography

- Primary font stack: KaiTi (楷体) family — always use the project's configured font stack
- Headings: h5 fontWeight 700, h6 fontWeight 600
- Never override the established typography system

### Component Patterns

- AppBar: gradient background `linear-gradient(135deg, #c44520 0%, #8a3016 100%)`
- Sidebar drawer: 240px width, persistent variant
- Active menu items: 4px left border in primary color with 8% primary background

## Rules

1. Always use MUI components from `@mui/material` — never install alternative UI libraries
2. Use react-admin components (List, Edit, Create, Show, etc.) for CRUD views
3. Use the `sx` prop for styling — avoid creating separate CSS files
4. Reference theme tokens via `theme.palette.*` or the `sx` system (e.g., `color: 'primary.main'`)
5. Use MUI Icons from `@mui/icons-material` — do not use other icon libraries
6. All user-facing text must be in Chinese (Simplified)
7. Maintain the warm cinnabar/gold aesthetic across all pages
8. Follow react-admin conventions for data providers, auth, and resource definitions
9. Responsive design: sidebar collapses on mobile, content adapts
10. Loading states: use MUI Skeleton components matching actual layout shape

## Anti-Patterns

- Do NOT use Tailwind CSS — this project uses MUI/Emotion exclusively
- Do NOT use shadcn/ui — this project uses MUI exclusively
- Do NOT hardcode colors — always reference theme palette tokens
- Do NOT create custom buttons when MUI Button variants exist
- Do NOT use `style={}` inline — use `sx={}` or `styled()`
- Do NOT import from `@mui/lab` without checking availability first
